COMMENT     The assembly wpHarImpa5.1 is based on 30x PacBio data and Arima2
            Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project
            (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included
            the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation
            with Hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with purge_dups, and
            Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was
            assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, the primary assembly was
            analysed and manually improved using gEVAL. Chromosome-scale
            scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of
            size. It appears that there are inversions between sister
            chromatids in the following approximate locations:Chromosome 1:
            54-69MbChromosome 2: 14-80MbChromosome 12: 22-64MbChromosome 14:
            20-60Mb.
